# The ledger of `i18n`: languages named and matched (BCP 47), CLDR's plural
# rules, and gettext's message catalogs. One block per capability, and what
# Heroes answers to each. Its subpackages keep their own ledgers:
# `i18n/numbers`, `i18n/dates`, `i18n/collate`, `i18n/locales`.
#
# The census, by the author's decision of 2026-11-17, is wider than README
# § A8's three libraries, since Go's and Rust's standard libraries hold no
# i18n: `go` is `golang.org/x/text` v0.14.0 (`go doc`, from a module cache
# of the round's scratch folder); `rust` is the crate `icu_locale_core` 2.4
# (its documentation; no source opened); `python` is Python 3.15.2's
# `gettext` and `locale` (`dir()`); `java` is Java SE 25's `java.util.Locale`,
# `java.util.ResourceBundle` and `java.text`; `dotnet` is .NET's
# `System.Globalization` and `System.Resources`; `odin` is Odin's
# `core:text/i18n`; `icu` is ICU 79.1, the yardstick, run on this machine
# (CLDR 49). Java, .NET and Odin were read from their documentation, none
# being on this machine: the census's unrun lists.

## Locales

capability locale/parse  a BCP 47 tag read into its parts, case made canonical
  heroes  i18n.parse_locale
  go      language.Parse, language.Make, language.MustParse, language.ParseBase, language.ParseScript, language.ParseRegion, language.ParseVariant, language.ParseExtension, language.Compose
  rust    Locale::try_from_str, LanguageIdentifier::try_from_str
  python  -
  java    Locale.forLanguageTag, Locale.Builder.setLanguageTag, Locale.Builder.setLanguage, Locale.Builder.setScript, Locale.Builder.setRegion, Locale.Builder.setVariant, Locale.Builder.setExtension, Locale.of, IllformedLocaleException
  dotnet  CultureInfo.GetCultureInfoByIetfLanguageTag, CultureInfo.GetCultureInfo, CultureInfo(String), CultureNotFoundException
  odin    -
  icu     ULocale.forLanguageTag, uloc_forLanguageTag
  note    `_` separates as `-` does, as ICU reads it; `root` is `und`; an extended language subtag stands for the language (`zh-yue` is `yue`), as ICU writes it; the irregular grandfathered tags take CLDR's replacements (`en-GB-oed` is `en-GB-oxendict`); a variant or singleton written twice is `invalid`, as Java refuses it

capability locale/format  a locale written as a BCP 47 tag
  heroes  i18n.format_locale
  go      Tag.String
  rust    Locale::to_string
  python  -
  java    Locale.toLanguageTag, Locale.toString
  dotnet  CultureInfo.Name, CultureInfo.IetfLanguageTag
  odin    -
  icu     ULocale.toLanguageTag, uloc_toLanguageTag
  note    extensions in the order of their singletons, as RFC 5646 § 4.5 asks

capability locale/parts  a tag's language, script, region, variants, extensions and private use
  heroes  i18n.Locale
  go      Tag.Base, Tag.Script, Tag.Region, Tag.Variants, Tag.Extensions, Tag.Extension, Tag.Raw, Tag.IsRoot, Tag.Parent, Base.String, Script.String, Region.String, Variant.String, Extension.String, Extension.Type, Extension.Tokens
  rust    Locale::id, LanguageIdentifier::language, LanguageIdentifier::script, LanguageIdentifier::region, LanguageIdentifier::variants, Locale::extensions
  python  -
  java    Locale.getLanguage, Locale.getScript, Locale.getCountry, Locale.getVariant, Locale.getExtension, Locale.getExtensionKeys, Locale.hasExtensions, Locale.stripExtensions
  dotnet  CultureInfo.TwoLetterISOLanguageName, RegionInfo.TwoLetterISORegionName, RegionInfo.Name
  odin    -
  icu     ULocale.getLanguage, ULocale.getScript, ULocale.getCountry, ULocale.getVariant

capability locale/posix  a POSIX locale name read and written
  heroes  i18n.parse_posix, i18n.format_posix
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  locale.normalize, locale.locale_alias, locale.windows_locale, locale.getlocale
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  odin    -
  icu     uloc_canonicalize
  note    the code set is dropped, a text being UTF-8 here; `C` and `POSIX` are `und`; Python's alias table, which guesses a code set per name, is not taken

capability locale/keywords  a Unicode locale keyword read and set: calendar, collation, numbering system, hour cycle
  heroes  i18n.unicode_keyword, i18n.with_unicode_keyword
  go      Tag.TypeForKey, Tag.SetTypeForKey
  rust    Locale::extensions.unicode.keywords
  python  -
  java    Locale.getUnicodeLocaleType, Locale.getUnicodeLocaleKeys, Locale.getUnicodeLocaleAttributes, Locale.Builder.setUnicodeLocaleKeyword, Locale.Builder.addUnicodeLocaleAttribute, Locale.Builder.removeUnicodeLocaleAttribute, Locale.Builder.clearExtensions
  dotnet  -
  odin    -
  icu     ULocale.getKeywordValue, ULocale.setKeywordValue, ULocale.getUnicodeLocaleType

capability locale/fallback  the locales a lookup falls back through, CLDR's parents
  heroes  i18n.parent_of, i18n.fallback_chain
  go      Tag.Parent
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    ResourceBundle.Control.getCandidateLocales, ResourceBundle.Control.getFallbackLocale
  dotnet  CultureInfo.Parent
  odin    -
  icu     ULocale.getFallback, uloc_getParent
  note    CLDR's parent locales (`en-AU` from `en-001`), a script other than the language's own going to the root, and a missing script added where the region chooses one (`zh-TW` is `zh-Hant-TW`); every subpackage finds its data through this chain

capability locale/accept-language  an HTTP Accept-Language header read into weighted ranges
  heroes  i18n.parse_accept_language
  go      language.ParseAcceptLanguage
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    Locale.LanguageRange.parse, Locale.LanguageRange.getRange, Locale.LanguageRange.getWeight, Locale.LanguageRange.mapEquivalents, Locale.LanguageRange.MAX_WEIGHT, Locale.LanguageRange.MIN_WEIGHT
  dotnet  -
  odin    -
  icu     LocaleMatcher.Builder.setSupportedLocalesFromListString
  note    ranges of equal weight keep the header's order; a weight of 0 is kept; Java's equivalent-ranges map is not offered

