capability locale/environment  the languages the environment asks messages in
  heroes  i18n.environment_languages
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  locale.getdefaultlocale, locale.getlocale
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  odin    -
  icu     -
  note    LANGUAGE, LC_ALL, LC_MESSAGES and LANG in gettext's order, as Python's `gettext.find` reads them

capability locale/system  the languages and the locale of the formats the person chose in the system's settings
  heroes  i18n.system_languages, i18n.system_locale, i18n.FAILED
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    Locale.getDefault
  dotnet  CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture, CultureInfo.CurrentCulture
  odin    -
  icu     uloc_getDefault
  note    through the platform layer's member `hero_locale` (`runtime/platform/hero_locale.c`): on macOS CoreFoundation's `CFLocaleCopyPreferredLanguages` and `CFLocaleCopyCurrent`, which read the user's preferences and not the environment, so a program started from the Finder speaks the person's language; on Windows `GetUserPreferredUILanguages` and `GetUserDefaultLocaleName` (Microsoft's reference, read 2026-11-23); elsewhere the environment, gettext's order for the languages and LC_ALL, LC_TIME, LC_NUMERIC, LC_MONETARY and LANG for the formats, and where it sets none systemd's `/etc/locale.conf` (locale.conf(5)). ICU's identifier is made BCP 47 by CLDR's keyword aliases (`cldr-bcp47`, the table `i18n/internal/keyword_tables`), `en_US@rg=itzzzz` being `en-US-u-rg-itzzzz`; a Windows sort becomes CLDR's collation where CLDR has one (Microsoft's "Sort Order Identifiers", read 2026-11-23, and the box's `EnumSystemLocalesEx` with `LOCALE_ALTERNATE_SORTS`, run 2026-11-23: fifteen sorts, of which `de` phone book, `es` traditional, `ja` and `zh` radical and stroke, `zh` stroke and `zh` Bopomofo have one). Java and ICU on POSIX read the environment and on Windows the same calls; .NET's CurrentUICulture is the first language of the display, CurrentCulture the regional format. Run on this Mac (macOS 27.2: `en-US`, `it-IT`, `it`, formats `en_US@rg=itzzzz`) and on the Windows box (`en-US`, formats `en-US`, from ssh and from the desktop session alike); the reading of `/etc/locale.conf` on a Linux machine is held by its cases alone, unrun on one

capability locale/set-default  the process's own locale changed
  heroes  refused: a process-wide locale is mutable state every thread reads (C's setlocale is not thread-safe); every function here takes its locale as an argument
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  locale.setlocale, locale.LC_ALL, locale.LC_COLLATE, locale.LC_CTYPE, locale.LC_MESSAGES, locale.LC_MONETARY, locale.LC_NUMERIC, locale.LC_TIME, locale.Error, locale.CHAR_MAX
  java    Locale.setDefault, Locale.Category
  dotnet  CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, CultureInfo.DefaultThreadCurrentCulture, CultureInfo.DefaultThreadCurrentUICulture
  odin    -
  icu     uloc_setDefault

capability locale/display-name  a language, script or region named in words in a language
  heroes  pending: CLDR's display names are its largest tables after annotations, 35 MB of JSON; not carried yet
  go      display.Tags, display.Languages, display.Scripts, display.Regions, display.Language, display.Region, display.Script, display.Tag, display.Self, display.Dictionary
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    Locale.getDisplayName, Locale.getDisplayLanguage, Locale.getDisplayScript, Locale.getDisplayCountry, Locale.getDisplayVariant
  dotnet  CultureInfo.DisplayName, CultureInfo.NativeName, CultureInfo.EnglishName, RegionInfo.DisplayName, RegionInfo.NativeName, RegionInfo.EnglishName
  odin    -
  icu     ULocale.getDisplayName, LocaleDisplayNames

capability locale/available  every locale CLDR has data for, and every ISO code
  heroes  pending: each subpackage reads its own list of locales and none is offered yet
  go      language.Supported, collate.Supported
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    Locale.getAvailableLocales, Locale.getISOCountries, Locale.getISOLanguages, Locale.IsoCountryCode
  dotnet  CultureInfo.GetCultures, CultureTypes
