## Plural rules

capability plural/cardinal  the plural category of a count in a language, CLDR's rules
  heroes  i18n.plural_rules, i18n.select_plural, i18n.plural_of, i18n.plural_of_int, i18n.Plural, i18n.PluralKind
  go      plural.Cardinal, plural.Rules.MatchPlural, plural.Form
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  odin    -
  icu     PluralRules.forLocale, PluralRules.select, uplrules_select
  note    a number is decimal text so that `1.0` is not `1`, as CLDR's operands read it; every sample CLDR gives every rule of every locale is a test

capability plural/ordinal  the ordinal category of a position
  heroes  i18n.ordinal_of
  go      plural.Ordinal
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  odin    -
  icu     PluralRules.forLocale(ORDINAL), uplrules_openForType

capability plural/custom  rules written by the program
  heroes  i18n.parse_plural_rules, i18n.PluralRules, i18n.PluralRule
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  odin    -
  icu     PluralRules.createRules, PluralRules.parseDescription, PluralRules.getRules, PluralRules.getSamples
  note    conditions compiled to flat programs; a condition is at most 1,000 bytes and a number at most 15 digits, so nothing overflows

capability plural/ranges  the category of a range "1-2 days"
