## Message catalogs

capability gettext/lookup  a message's translation, with its context and plural forms
  heroes  i18n.translate, i18n.translate_in, i18n.translate_plural, i18n.translate_plural_in, i18n.find_message, i18n.find_message_in
  go      message.Printer.Sprintf, message.SetString, message.Set, catalog.Builder.SetString, catalog.Builder.Set, catalog.Catalog.Matcher, catalog.String, catalog.Var, plural.Selectf, catalog.ErrNotFound
  rust    -
  python  gettext.gettext, gettext.ngettext, gettext.pgettext, gettext.npgettext, gettext.dgettext, gettext.dngettext, gettext.dpgettext, gettext.dnpgettext, GNUTranslations.gettext, GNUTranslations.ngettext, GNUTranslations.pgettext, GNUTranslations.npgettext, NullTranslations.gettext, NullTranslations.ngettext, NullTranslations.pgettext, NullTranslations.npgettext
  java    ResourceBundle.getString, ResourceBundle.getObject, ResourceBundle.getStringArray, ResourceBundle.containsKey, ResourceBundle.keySet, ResourceBundle.getKeys, MissingResourceException
  dotnet  ResourceManager.GetString, ResourceManager.GetObject, ResourceSet.GetString
  odin    i18n.get, i18n.get_single_section, i18n.get_by_section, i18n.get_by_slot, i18n.get_single_section_by_slot
  note    a fuzzy, obsolete or untranslated message is no translation, as msgfmt leaves it out; a missing translation is the program's own text, 1 and -1 taking the singular; an expression that fails takes the first form, as GNU gettext does

capability gettext/mo-read  a .mo file read
  heroes  i18n.decode_mo
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  GNUTranslations, GNUTranslations.LE_MAGIC, GNUTranslations.BE_MAGIC, GNUTranslations.VERSIONS, GNUTranslations.CONTEXT, gettext.Catalog
  java    -
  dotnet  -
  odin    i18n.parse_mo_file, i18n.parse_mo_from_bytes
  icu     -
  note    both byte orders, revisions 0 and 1; a character set other than UTF-8 is `unsupported` where a string leaves ASCII (decode it with `unicode/encodings` first)

capability gettext/mo-write  a .mo file written
